  "result": "Perfect! The VAT report feature is complete and all tests pass. Here's what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Added `vatSummary(invoices)` to `src/reports.js`** that:\n- Filters for invoices with status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid' (excludes draft invoices)\n- Iterates through all lines and calculates the VAT base (line amount after discount) and VAT amount for each rate\n- Aggregates totals by VAT rate using a Map\n- Returns an array of objects with `{ rate, base, vat }` sorted by rate in descending order (high to low)\n- Uses banker's rounding via `roundCents` for precise VAT calculations\n\n**Added 19 comprehensive tests to `test/reports.test.js`** covering:\n- Empty invoice arrays and empty line arrays\n- Status filtering (draft excluded, issued/partially_paid/paid included)\n- Single and multiple VAT rates\n- Discount application to the VAT base\n- Aggregation across multiple invoices\n- Sorting by rate descending\n- Default VAT rate of 0 for missing vatRate\n- Edge cases: zero VAT, very large amounts, decimal discount percentages\n- Complex scenarios with multiple rates and discounts\n\n**Results:** All 278 tests pass (259 existing + 19 new).",
